{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/52206-storytellers-only-sothic-turn-0-and-the-first-memories-of-a-mummy","id":52206,"title":"(Storytellers Only) Sothic Turn 0, and the First Memories of a Mummy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-18T00:59:49-08:00","id":52206,"title":"(Storytellers Only) Sothic Turn 0, and the First Memories of a Mummy","content":"I recall, once upon a time, that the developers mentioned SIX Sothic turns, rather than four, in the context of the mummy game. In the process of doing far too much Wikipedia research, I began to see a pattern emerging around the Sothic turn JUST prior to the first mentioned in the book, when IRL most culture was beginning to emerge. The developers say that Irem and its mythos is more or less anchored into the real life history of this world. When the book of Sothis, mummy endgame and history more or less clarified comes out, I hope they do some details on Sothic turns beyond the one in 2371, as well as what a Mummy might remember of its &quot;first life&quot; as a Mummy. Id also like more clarity his first life as a citizen of the Nameless Empire. Until then, we basically have to wing it in case Mummies grow in Memory faster than the books come out.<br /> <br /> My interest piqued when I researched the Sothic Turn prior to the &quot;First&quot; outlined in the Mummy core book. And Frankly? It looks like it was still AFTER Irem. While it is so far back into history it is unlikely any Mummy will remember it until endgame, the Sothic Turn of 3831 BC still seems to be after Irem. I mean.. if cities like Jericho existed for almost ten thousand years.. and agriculture and &quot;villages&quot; have existed for even longer.. how could the Shan'Iatu claim to have been the ones to give the light of civilization to mankind? Unless, perhaps.. Irem is far older, and far larger, than we thought.<br /> <br /> After all, the proto-indo-europeans were supposedly the ones who tamed horses. Did they steal the technology from Irem, or the other way around? And Mummies in India and China don't feel alien among the cultures that would've been the Indus River and Yellow River cultures at the Sothic Turn 0, far from the conservative estimates of Irem\u2018s extent. Most mummies remember the conquest of Mesopotamia/Kir-En-Gar, and the Iremite Silk Road. Most mummies remember having the same tamed horses as the barbarians from the northlands. And by that Sothic turn, the Naquada culture already was in full swing in its modern archaeological context. Surely, mummies must be older.<br /> <br /> They've always said MUMMIES are six thousand years old. I am beginning to think that the 3831 BC Sothic turn was the &quot;first life&quot; of mummies.. when they first woke from Duat, and may have literally had NO idea how to grasp what had happened to them, considering the worst implications of the Storytellers secrets (Such as the notion that Mummies may have been the ones that FAILED the rite of Return to become Judges). This would've been a huge, formative time in history, especially if the Shan'Iatu decided a Mummy should be entombed in distant Harrapa, or across the Black Sea or Mediterranean, or in the jungles found at the Nile's Heart and westward in the Kongo.<br /> <br /> And what about before that? Clearly, Irem is much older than most of us give it credit for. Its possible it was so thoroughly erased from time that everyone left behind was almost primitive, and from our archaeological perspective almost seemed to put together societies from nothing.. when really, they just revived Irem in their own ways. Was it as far as distant China? Or the Indo European Culture of the Steppes? Was Jericho one of the cities that Irem built, or did the Shan'Iatu try to hide the notions of ten thousand year old cities older than their influence? Was Irem there when the black sea flooded, or when the volcanic eruptions at the heart of the Mediterranean caused tsunamis and whiped out coasts and islands? Was it there before the Sahara was even a desert? Was it OLDER than the civilizations of Indus River and Yellow River? Or are they ALL Irem, ALL remembering the River?<br /> <br /> Did Irem have many dynasties? Did it survive multiple Sothic Turns? How many of the ancient myths of the world, such as the Tower of Babel, the Great Flood, refer to it? Did Irem cross the mountains of Central Asia into China and India? And considering how relatively easy the Black Sea, Bosporos, and Caucasus mountains would've been compared to Kir-En-Gar and the great Persian and Central Asian terrain.. did they control the &quot;Kurgans&quot;, too?<br /> <br /> I'd imagine any Mummy would awaken from Duat, for the first time, at Memory Zero.. then slowly rise to one, and need EXP to get higher.. Thus, they do not fully understand or remember Irem, even then, and may fabricate their own history based on where they wake up, and who talks to them. This then suggests that there are Mummies out there who never &quot;got over the hump&quot; at Memory 3, and have always been below. However, it lets you explore very old memories while still withholding solid information about Irem.<br /> <br /> This could evolve into an interesting storyteller discussion on history, and how we can apply it to the Mummy game. Anyone have other theories? Or thoughts of Irem's location, or how old and large it was? Or even what Mummies might be remembering in Year Zero, their first awakening as a Mummy? Not from a PC standpoint, strictly Storyteller thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 01-18-2014, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T05:04:19-08:00","id":52299,"title":"","content":"I recall a Mummy writer saying on rpg.net (I think) that when the Arisen first woke up they were at Memory 1. Memory 0 seems to be more of an &quot;emergency reset button&quot; than anything else, especially considering that, after returning to Duat at Memory 0, their next Descent the Mummy will return to Memory 1. This implies that the Judges deem it acceptable for their servants to be at Memory 1 but no higher","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T17:56:36-08:00","id":52889,"title":"","content":"I was only referring to the first scene or so of any descent when they start at 0, then drift upwards. They'd end up at one, and need exp to get higher. Which means even then, so close to Irem, theyd have to piece everything together. Then again, at their first life as a mummy.. would they unlock their previous life's memories at the same time as mummies remember their last descent? Or would they have to rise to the level to unlock their memories of life, like all deathless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T10:41:07-08:00","id":54758,"title":"","content":"If you want to really get your noodle turning, check out this bit on pg34:<br /> <br /> &quot;At the Empire\u2019s height, the engravers crafted a huge marble seal that was capable of raining Sekhem on multiple Arisen all the way out to the horizon. When it was taken, the Amkhat army feasted for days.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's never brought up again, so I'm uncertain whether it's an error, a remnant of prior versions of the game, or a sneak teaser about the direction of future books. It does seem to contradict the bit earlier, on pg21:<br /> <br /> &quot;No mummy arose during the time of Irem, not even the very first of those subjected to the Rite. They lay as withered corpses through the Nameless Empire\u2019s end.&quot;<br /> <br /> That whole section seems to imply that it took some time after their creation for the Rite of Return to finish &quot;taking&quot; and the first Arising to have been beyond &quot;Sothic Turn 0&quot;. But there's no reason you couldn't tweak that on your own and add a secret &quot;Sothic Turn 0&quot; that Mummies who haven't gone through apotheosis can't remember, during which they fought to defend the last remnants of the Nameless Empire against the tide of destruction manifested by Ammut after the Shan'iatu made their sacrifice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1772-egarwaen","name":"Egarwaen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T14:09:11-08:00","id":54888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egarwaen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/52206-storytellers-only-sothic-turn-0-and-the-first-memories-of-a-mummy?p=54758#post54758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to really get your noodle turning, check out this bit on pg34: &quot;At the Empire\u2019s height, the engravers crafted a huge marble seal that was capable of raining Sekhem on multiple Arisen all the way out to the horizon. When it was taken, the Amkhat army feasted for days.&quot; It's never brought up again, so I'm uncertain whether it's an error, a remnant of prior versions of the game, or a sneak teaser about the direction of future books. It does seem to contradict the bit earlier, on pg21: &quot;No mummy arose during the time of Irem, not even the very first of those subjected to the Rite. They lay as withered corpses through the Nameless Empire\u2019s end.&quot; That whole section seems to imply that it took some time after their creation for the Rite of Return to finish &quot;taking&quot; and the first Arising to have been beyond &quot;Sothic Turn 0&quot;. But there's no reason you couldn't tweak that on your own and add a secret &quot;Sothic Turn 0&quot; that Mummies who haven't gone through apotheosis can't remember, during which they fought to defend the last remnants of the Nameless Empire against the tide of destruction manifested by Ammut after the Shan'iatu made their sacrifice.</div> </div> </div> </div> It really comes down to just WHEN the empire fell. I previously assumed it wouldve been the sothic turn prior to the 2000bc one (that is, it fell in my turn 0). However, reading the history made me wonder if it was not older than that. By the sothic turn 0, much of the world was growing independently already. Unless, of course, the archaeology hasn't made the link between the empire's nations yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}